save(417,dict(paragraphs=["Gayatri Mavuru is a poet, artist, educator and translator. Her collection Sizzling Verses: Drizzling Colours appears in the Guntur International Poetry Festival’s record of book releases. Outlook has also published her English translation of Tirupati Kiran’s Telugu story ‘Lives in the Shadows’.","In ‘The Burden of Creation’, her poem in Kabita Live, artistic work becomes both a struggle and a source of renewal. Pigment, canvas, brushstroke and clay give physical form to doubt and persistence. The repeated act of carrying gathers failures and moments of wonder into the same life, moving towards a quiet reconciliation between the maker and what is made."],sources=[source('Guntur International Poetry Festival — Books released','https://www.gipf.club/books-releasing-at-12-gipf',['Sizzling Verses Drizzling Colours by Gayatri Mavuru listed as a book release.']),source('Outlook — Lives in the Shadows','https://www.outlookindia.com/culture-society/lives-in-the-shadows',['Translation credit from Telugu original by Tirupati Kiran; contributor biography identifies poet, artist and educator.'])],identity_match='Distinctive full name, artist/educator roles and collection title match captured biography; Outlook publishes explicit translator credit.',poems_read=[dict(id=617,title='The Burden of Creation',basis='Full original read: repeated I carry; pigment/canvas, failed visions, brushstrokes, grace, clay, creative reconciliation and mortality.')],limitations=['Captured biography separates Sizzling Verses and Drizzling Colours; festival listing and bibliographic record treat them as one title/subtitle. New narrative uses combined title while preserving capture.','World-record, honorary-degree and award claims not independently verified and omitted.','Current principal role not verified with school; omitted. No verified book product URL added.'],next_action='Author/editor confirm preferred book-title punctuation and factual biography.'))
